  "question": {
    "text": "An artificial satellite is made to move in circular orbits of different radii around the earth. The variations of its K.E., P.E. and total energy (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math>) in different orbits is shown in the figure by different curves.<br />\rThen for the satellites<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image8-d52f3a8c-9b4f-4a68-acb2-e0ea429a80e1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"height: 194px; width: 200px;\" />",
